WEBVTT

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:03.670
In the vastness of space,

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:07.480
the probability of a meeting between any two people

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.440
is so unimaginably low

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.490
that it can only be called fate.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.620
Coincidences accrue,

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.330
eventually becoming an inevitable future.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.400
The bonds between people cross over light itself.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:26.040
Actually, I have a job for the Bentenmaru.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:27.540
A job?

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:34.010
I wish to kidnap the former president of the
Hakuoh Academy Yacht Club, Jenny Dolittle.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.010
What's going to happen now?

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.480
Kidnap Jenny?

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.850
What do you mean?

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.610
To be precise, it's a pick-up job disguised as a kidnapping.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:16.150
Jenny agreed to it.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:18.570
Rather,

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.780
she's actually the one hiring you.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.080
The ship heading to Diment is the Central Lanes liner,

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.120
Ultimate Fairy.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.210
I want you to get Jenny off of it.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.250
Then the person you've been speaking to...

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:33.500
It was Jenny.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:36.300
We were discussing the best way to hire you.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:40.220
As a fellow pirate, let me be clear.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:44.720
Pirates cannot actually commit crimes.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:51.690
We can only engage in piracy due to our contracts
with liners and insurance companies.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:56.360
I finally understood that during this trip.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.820
You aren't just a bunch of raiders.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:01.280
Really, you're very careful.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:05.080
That's why I want to hire the Bentenmaru.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:06.740
Marika already knows us well,

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.250
and she is a talented captain.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.630
You flatter me, President.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:17.460
So why are we kidnapping Jenny?

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:24.180
You know her family is part of the large
transport company Hugh and Dolittle, right?

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:26.350
Yes, I'd heard that.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:34.520
For a family-run business, Hugh and Dolittle
Interstellar Transportation is extremely aggressive.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.360
I'm impressed you knew that.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.820
I only know the basics.

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:44.070
The company marries its employees' children to
politicians or executives at major companies,

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.080
in order to expand its business.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:50.910
Jenny is to be married to a politician.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:57.340
Well, it'd normally be a good thing.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:02.880
The problem is that she doesn't want to marry,
and a lot is going on behind the scenes.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:03.800
Behind the scenes?

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:11.430
Jenny's a candidate to inherit the company, but her uncle, the current managing director, wants his son to inherit it.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:17.230
He plans to marry her off to some politician
in order to remove her from the company.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:18.360
I see now.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:22.530
So he considers her that big of a threat?

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:26.820
She actually started her own small company.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:31.250
But at the moment, she can't devote any time to it.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.210
She wants to go to Space University.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.170
Space University?

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.040
Where elite students from all over the universe go?

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.540
Yeah.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:42.260
She studied hard over the summer, and she passed the exam.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:45.690
She wants to learn more about running
a company, and how to make connections.

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:46.890
Sounds just like her.

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:50.310
Here is the job.

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:54.850
Get Jenny off that liner, and take her to Space University.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.820
Space University is extralegal territory.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:05.950
Once you're a student there, not even a fleet or army can remove you easily.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:07.280
Please, Marika!

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.130
Who are you people?!

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.270
Kidnap Jenny?

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.520
Wow, that sounds fun!

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.020
Now we're doing real pirate stuff!

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:41.440
It's for the president... No, for Jenny!

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.530
We have to do it, right?

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:43.990
Yeah!

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.440
Excuse me...

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:48.200
What's Jenny like?

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.490
You'll know once you meet her.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.950
She has this amazing aura.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.200
She's pretty,

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:54.660
but absolutely strong willed...

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:55.450
That's right.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:57.670
She got mad at me a lot.

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:59.040
But it was always out of love.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:00.920
I can't wait to meet her.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:03.170
That's what I thought they'd say.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:08.260
When you asked them to crew the
Bentenmaru, they agreed to that too.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:10.510
It's wonderful. Right, President Lynn?

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:11.890
Yeah.

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:14.890
I'm sorry, but I'm against it.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:19.190
Ad-lib work is too dangerous.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.020
You're all novices.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:24.440
You've all become overexcited because you
managed to pilot the ship and do a little piracy.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:33.160
To extract her, you'll need various kinds of plans and processes.

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:37.000
Even if you can get her out, you may need to fight.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.080
Have you considered that?

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:43.340
You may well lose your pirate license too.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.710
Will you do it regardless?

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:52.600
Doesn't it sound fun though?

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:57.980
Taking Jenny away from there and all.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:02.060
Staying within the lines is nice, but it isn't enough.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:04.190
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:08.280
As pirates, we only keep our jobs by staying within the lines.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.410
But I think too much job security can be bad.

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:15.910
We're pirates, and that isn't very pirate-like.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:21.460
I'm taking this job.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:27.920
Very well.

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:31.880
Okay, now that it's decided,

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:36.500
let's trace the route the Ultimate Fairy,
the Central Lanes liner heading to Diment, took

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:37.600
and make our plans!

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:39.310
Okay!

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:47.150
Oh, here it is.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:47.530
Pirate News

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.150
It's an article on the Bentenmaru from yesterday.

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:51.200
It reads "Cosplay Pirates Appear!"

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:54.320
They look pretty good.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:57.990
"A rare performance by the very traditional Bentenmaru..."

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.750
Well, that's true.

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:03.710
I'm glad it went okay, but I'm not sure how I feel about the rest.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:06.460
They did really well, though.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:10.380
Looks like they got alpha and beta working in synch.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.760
Maybe they have a good engineer.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.470
Well, now they only need to return.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.300
And everything will have worked out.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:19.430
Silver falling stars.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:24.500
Caught in a dark spiral, Southgarty will be helpless before a power

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:27.480
greater than any it has previously faced.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.940
What does that mean?

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:32.400
No idea.

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:40.910
Something's approaching the Bentenmaru!

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:43.000
Can you identify it?

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:43.620
Working on it.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.710
It's five million kilometers behind us.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:48.670
It's a small ship, flying by impulse,
with transponder systems off.

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:49.630
Any communications?

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:51.420
They're switched off now,

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:54.180
but it did send a message requesting assistance.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:55.840
It's Jenny!

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:58.180
But weren't we supposed to kidnap her?

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:00.510
I thought so...

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.980
Something unexpected must've happened.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.230
Maybe she boarded that small ship to fly to us.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:11.280
This morning, I sent her the Bentenmaru's location just in case.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:15.030
I don't fully understand,
but there's only one thing for us to do.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:17.570
Everyone, to your stations!

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.160
We must recover that ship now.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.620
Got it?

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:34.720
It's an electronic-recon vessel: a Liosen Gelyune Silent Whisper.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:38.010
The Imperial Fleet just began deploying those.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.600
They're a brand new model of spaceship, correct?

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:44.980
They've only been sold to wealthy
corporations and stellar navies so far.

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:47.810
We recently acquired one a short while ago.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:54.990
She said she'd be in a small ship with an FTL booster,
but I didn't expect military-grade.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:59.530
She must have chosen something that would
guarantee her escape in case of pursuit.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:01.530
Jenny's smart after all.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.800
The ship is inside.

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:17.260
Roger.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:21.300
Captain, a word.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.100
Listen,

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:26.500
they've completely taken the lead on this.

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:27.530
Is that all right?

00:10:27.530 --> 00:10:29.060
They sure have.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:29.850
You seriously...

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:33.020
I told you. It sounded fun.

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:34.440
Let's just go with it.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:38.200
Well, you're the captain.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:39.160
But don't blame me for whatever happens.

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.870
Thanks for your concern.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:52.420
Jenny!

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:53.340
Lynn!

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:56.340
Come here.

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:02.340
J-Jenny?

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:07.220
Welcome back.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.190
I've returned.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.350
What happened?

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:48.180
I told you we'd come to get you.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:50.140
Well, you see...

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:11.410
So I ran away.

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:15.460
I know you had a whole plan worked out.

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:16.380
I'm sorry.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:20.090
No, I'm glad you weren't hurt.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:26.550
U-Um...

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:29.770
Everyone's watching.

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.770
Just let them watch!

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:34.480
We shouldn't.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:40.400
I'm sorry for not saying hello, Captain.

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:44.360
I, Jenny Dolittle, request permission to board the Bentenmaru.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:47.990
I-I am captain of the Bentenmaru, Kato Marika.

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:49.870
Permission is granted, of course.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:52.540
So you two are in a relationship?

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:56.130
Well, I guess so.

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:58.180
Did you arrange this to elope, President?

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:01.010
No, it's actually unrelated.

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:05.990
Nothing on the radar.

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:07.430
Expanding the search radius.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:10.060
You still can't locate Jenny?

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:14.510
Sh-She's turned off her transponder and radio.

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:18.610
We caught a single message she sent to a ship.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:19.650
Which one?

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:21.650
The pirate ship Bentenmaru.

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:24.860
The Bentenmaru?

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:27.780
Find their insurance company.

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:29.070
We'll pressure them there.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:38.040
Honestly, this is just weird.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:39.250
What is?

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:43.310
The Bentenmaru has picked up a small spaceship.

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:44.970
A small spaceship?

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:46.760
A Silent Whisper.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:48.930
The new model?

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:49.470
Wow.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:50.930
Oh, really?

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.430
The falling silver star.

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:58.900
Let me introduce you all.

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:01.940
This is the former yacht club president,
Jenny Dolittle.

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.200
It's good to see you again, Jenny.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:07.150
Have you been well?

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:10.120
Yes, and I'm glad to see you've all been well.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:11.370
Jenny!

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:14.540
These are our new members.

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:16.160
H-Hello.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:17.830
I'm honored to meet you.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:18.830
Hello there!

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.090
Nice to meet you too.

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:23.210
Help Lynn out, okay?

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:24.420
Of course.

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:32.300
Captain, a message from the Harold Lloyd Insurance Union.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:32.850
What should we do?

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:34.600
I'll answer it.

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:41.770
Hey, it's your buddy at the Harold Lloyd Insurance Union, Show.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:44.780
I was just about to contact you.

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:48.200
I need to confirm a few things with you.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:53.080
Is Jenny Dolittle of Hugh and Dolittle Interstellar Transportation with you?

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:54.700
How did you know?

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:56.160
Oh, no!

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:57.120
She really is?!

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:59.210
Um, what's up?

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:02.420
That's what I want to know.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:11.590
I just got a message from the Hugh and Dolittle company fleet that the Bentenmaru kidnapped her.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:18.270
My uncle is behind this.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:19.560
I see.

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:21.690
Then you're Jenny Dolittle?

00:15:22.030 --> 00:15:23.810
Yes, it's nice to meet you.

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:27.150
The information you've been given is a lie.

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:29.110
Oh, is it?

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:33.740
This entire thing originated with a rift between my uncle and me.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:40.460
I've hired the Bentenmaru to secure my safety.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.210
All right.

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:50.010
Well, if you were planning a pirate kidnapping,
the captain should have spoken with us first.

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.720
Sorry.

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.260
We've been busy here.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:55.600
So here's the thing...

00:15:55.600 --> 00:15:57.180
Your uncle,

00:15:57.180 --> 00:16:00.180
Robert Dolittle, demands your immediate release.

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:03.650
If we don't comply, he's threatening to cut ties with our company.

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:08.900
That's just the kind of dirty trick he'd think up.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.850
Her eyes aren't laughing.

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:22.500
Show, I haven't actually negotiated payment with her.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:31.970
Will you observe our discussion before deciding if you'll hand her over?

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:38.600
Don't you have a little time
to decide which side you'll take?

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:41.180
Very well.

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:46.020
I hate to bring it up with you, Jenny,

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.230
but this is business.

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:50.280
It's fine.

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:52.440
That makes it easier for me.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:56.030
Then let's get started.

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:59.120
What is our payment for this job?

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:02.290
The Silent Whisper's registration.

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:04.580
You can take that for the advance.

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.330
Name it whatever you like.

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:14.680
And ten percent of the gross profit from my interstellar
travel company, Fairy Jane, for the next ten years.

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.550
That will be your compensation.

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:21.270
Fairy Jane is one of the fastest
growing travel companies around.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:24.520
Ten percent of fifty trillion per year...

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:28.480
That's half the royal palace's annual budget.

00:17:28.860 --> 00:17:33.190
The commission the insurance company
receives would be quite sizable as well.

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:40.330
I'll throw in some of my personally collected data.

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:46.120
Customer lists, information on pirate ships, corporate trade secrets.

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:47.620
I see.

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:53.880
In the future, it's quite possible that Fairy Jane will end up being a bigger company than Hugh and Dolittle.

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:56.510
It's currently one of a group of companies.

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:58.090
But should it go independent...

00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:04.810
For our part, I think that's a better deal than bowing to some guiling pressure.

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:09.810
Man, you girls are gonna be scary in ten years.

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:11.920
Fine.

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:13.820
I'll give you my personal decision.

00:18:18.570 --> 00:18:22.780
I'd like to permit the Bentenmaru to undertake the job.

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:24.120
Really?!

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:31.750
Thank you.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:37.970
I'm not a big fan of the "do what we want, or we'll drop you" trick.

00:18:38.970 --> 00:18:43.470
But even though I'm part of a big company,
I'd still like to prevent that.

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:45.640
Then let's take them out.

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:51.650
That would both solve your arranged marriage problem

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:54.980
and relieve the pressure on our insurance company.

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:57.740
That's true.

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:01.570
He is a relative, so I hadn't considered that.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.410
But we should finish this.

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:08.710
It won't be long before the Hugh and Dolittle fleet finds the Bentenmaru.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:10.800
Let's head for Space University

00:19:10.800 --> 00:19:12.670
while we formulate a plan.

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:15.880
Hey, Bentenmaru crew!

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:18.170
Ya'll are wondering what Captain Marika is up to, right?

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:22.220
You're late!

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:24.350
So what's happening?

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:25.560
They picked up that ship, right?

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:28.680
If you know that much, this'll be quick.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:32.730
Jenny Dolittle was on board the ship.

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:38.320
She requested their protection as an escort,
and the Bentenmaru has formally accepted.

00:19:38.580 --> 00:19:40.900
Protection and escort?

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:43.200
They're doing more work?

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:45.280
Yup. Just like us adults.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:47.200
Is this all right?

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:50.660
Jenny used to be president of the yacht club.

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:53.040
She's part of the Hugh and Dolittle company, right?

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.210
That's right!

00:19:55.210 --> 00:20:00.170
And it's Hugh and Dolittle that they're up against.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.300
They've been accused of kidnapping.

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:05.760
Jeez... The captain always does the craziest stuff.

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:08.430
That's a pretty big job.

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:12.730
You were there. Why did you let her take it?

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:16.440
I guess I believed in her luck and potential.

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:18.860
How irresponsible...

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:21.240
Not that I mind.

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:26.830
If she can pull this off, there's a lot in it for the Bentenmaru.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:30.770
I think that's probably the reason why she took the job.

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:35.170
I'll contact you when there's an update.

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:36.080
Peace!

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:49.850
The Hugh and Dolittle fleet is at
five hundred kilometers and closing!

00:20:50.340 --> 00:20:51.850
Let's draw them in as close as possible, then jump.

00:20:52.220 --> 00:20:53.340
Got it?

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:54.640
I'm counting on you, Ai!

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:56.060
I'll dodge them somehow.

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:58.270
We should get them to let us out!

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:01.650
No, the negotiations would take several days.

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:02.240
There isn't time.

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:05.490
Let's get out of here!

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:08.580
We'll find a ship somehow, and get to the Bentenmaru...

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:09.080
Wait.

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:15.960
Until Marika contacts us, we should stay here.

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:18.170
We don't have time for that!

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:19.210
That's our ship!

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:21.960
Marika is the captain.

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:31.220
Stupid girl.

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:36.980
We'll execute a short-range jump
so they can't follow our wake.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:40.440
Take us to the center of whichever
lane will be easiest to hide in.

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:42.400
Sending coordinates.

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:44.110
Got it.

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:45.610
How are the reactors?

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:48.200
Energy supply is okay.

00:21:48.200 --> 00:21:49.870
We can do an FTL jump.

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:52.410
Okay, let's do it.

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:53.970
Faster than light jump!

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:08.260
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:11.220
A Surprising Client

00:22:11.220 --> 00:22:12.470
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:12.470 --> 00:22:17.980
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:17.980 --> 00:22:20.980
Welcome glory, let's breakthrough and fly out now, let's go!

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:24.360
Run towards an unlimited dimension. Come, let's accelerate beyond this

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:27.450
history that's to be known, regardless of time. Fly towards a destined future.

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:30.490
Just a fossil if you give up a miracle. Your decision is your best choice.

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:39.420
There's another, unknown, me hiding in my heart.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:44.300
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:48.130
How far?

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:50.800
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell! Go, go, ring, ring a bell!

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:54.430
Until the end.

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:55.770
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell!

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:59.100
You're lost and missing.

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:07.940
We're lost without a hope of any shelter.

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:11.700
But why? What did we do? What did we do?

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:13.120
What should we do?

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:16.290
From the world beyond shadows invade.

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:20.580
We're destined to stop them with our lives.

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:26.630
So no matter where we go, as far as it takes

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:30.880
we'll always believe in ourselves.

00:23:40.050 --> 00:23:41.850
The Bentenmaru flees,

00:23:41.850 --> 00:23:43.770
pursued by Hugh and Dolittle's company fleet.

00:23:44.860 --> 00:23:47.440
The inexperienced yacht club
fights as hard as they can.

00:23:47.900 --> 00:23:50.280
Captain Marika displays the
stubbornness of a pirate,

00:23:50.280 --> 00:23:52.700
in order to make Lynn and Jenny's dream come true.

00:23:54.020 --> 00:23:55.800
Next time, on <i>Bodacious Space Pirates:</i>

00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:57.620
We'll have juice at the after party.

00:23:57.620 --> 00:23:58.950
Look forward to it.

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:04.960
We'll Have Juice at the After Party

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:10.460
Then let's take them out.
